  "summary": "New preprints resolve neurodegeneration by cell type, age and stage, from synaptic proteomes to somatic mutation, interactomes and variant function.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is high-resolution molecular profiling of neurodevelopmental and neurodegenerative disease, with several items emphasizing age or stage. In R6/1 Huntington mice, cell-type proteomics shows excitatory synaptic protein loss and reduced glial neuronal support before motor onset, while aged TgHD minipig putamen shows age-dependent transcript and protein changes, including reduced D2 neuron markers. In ALS motor cortex, neuronal somatic mutation burden is higher in younger donors, with an SBS5 signature. A TDP-43 APEX2 atlas finds interactome remodelling persisting after stress granule clearance. A GBA1 assay maps glucocerebrosidase activity for over 10,400 variants. SETX loss in iPSC motor neurons shows stage-dependent effects, and 22q11.2 neurons show reversible mitophagy deficits. Fmr1-KO synapse profiling adds cell type-specific remodelling. Not all items concern aging.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-20"
}
